From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MinsOS <minsos@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Allow the second face template on the face HIDL HAL (One UI 9, y2q)

FaceEnrollClient.hasReachedEnrollmentLimit() caps a HIDL face HAL at one
template when SemBiometricFeature.FEATURE_JDM_HAL is set and at two otherwise,
the same rule as the stock SM-G986N A13 face/hidl/FaceEnrollClient. y2q sets
MANUFACTURING_TYPE=jdm only so that HidlToAidlSensorAdapter loads the V2_0 HAL
class, and that also took away the second template, the "alternative look":
enroll ended with "Reached enrollment limit" before the HAL was called. Stock
y2q is in_house (two templates), and its face@2.0 HAL itself refuses a third
(libFaceService.so FaceService::initEnroll, count < 2). Read the flag as false
in this method only.
---
diff --git a/smali/com/android/server/biometrics/sensors/face/aidl/FaceEnrollClient.smali b/smali/com/android/server/biometrics/sensors/face/aidl/FaceEnrollClient.smali
--- a/smali/com/android/server/biometrics/sensors/face/aidl/FaceEnrollClient.smali
+++ b/smali/com/android/server/biometrics/sensors/face/aidl/FaceEnrollClient.smali
@@ -150,7 +150,7 @@
 
     move-result p0
 
-    sget-boolean v0, Lcom/android/server/biometrics/SemBiometricFeature;->FEATURE_JDM_HAL:Z
+    const/4 v0, 0x0
 
     if-eqz v0, :cond_0
 
-- 
